         recommended test: A test is added that verifies an obligation whose quotation lies within its attributed requirement span remains attributed to that requirement.
           inputs:  Use two requirements whose text both contain the same quoted phrase, but attribute the obligation to the later requirement. The quoted text must appear verbatim in both requirements so a naive global search would find the first requirement first, while the correct implementation must keep the obligation with the attributed requirement because its own span contains the quote.
           detects: A developer only checks the attributed requirement first and never searches other requirements, so quotations from a different requirement are not re-attributed.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-obligation-keeps-own-span

